+## Deployment
+
+Fizzy includes a Kamal configuration for deploying to a single Linux server
+running Docker. SQLite, uploads, and background jobs all run on the one box,
+and SSL is handled by Kamal's proxy. See the
+[Deployment guide](docs/deployment.md) for instructions. In short:
+
+1. Fill in your server, hostname, and SMTP settings in `config/deploy.yml`.
+2. Provide `SECRET_KEY_BASE`, `SMTP_PASSWORD`, and optional VAPID keys through
+   `.kamal/secrets` (or the environment it reads them from).
+3. Run `bin/kamal setup`, then visit `https://your-hostname`.
+
+
